{% comment %}
  ZeroStick 8K — business-inquiry page (the "8K for Business" tab).

  The 8K controller is finished, so this page turned from a coming-soon
  teaser into a B2B page: other companies can buy Lightning boards in
  bulk, integrate them into their own products (OEM), or resell.

  Layout: the same full-bleed PCB hero (our own inline-SVG render), a
  short "the board is finished" mission, the four-card feature strip,
  three ways-to-work-with-us cards, a business-inquiry form (Shopify
  contact form — submissions email the store inbox), a B2B FAQ, and
  fine print. All styles scoped under .zx8; the hero is deliberately
  self-coloured (a PCB is a PCB in any theme scheme).
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  .zx8{ line-height:1.6; }
  .zx8 .hero{ position:relative; background:#05070c; }
  .zx8 .hero svg{ display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
  .zx8 .inner{ max-width:110rem; margin:0 auto; padding:0 2rem; }
  .zx8 h2{ margin:4.4rem 0 1rem; }
  .zx8 h3{ margin:0 0 .6rem; }
  .zx8 .mission{ font-size:1.7rem; opacity:.85; max-width:76rem; margin:3.2rem auto 0; }
  .zx8 .mission p{ margin:0 0 1.2rem; }
  .zx8 .strip{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(22rem,1fr));
    gap:1.4rem; margin:2rem 0; }
  .zx8 .feat{ border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.14);
    border-radius:1.2rem; padding:1.8rem 2rem; }
  .zx8 .feat .ico{ font-size:2rem; line-height:1; margin-bottom:.8rem; color:#58a6ff; }
  .zx8 .feat p{ margin:0; opacity:.75; font-size:1.4rem; }
  .zx8 .ways{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(24rem,1fr));
    gap:1.4rem; margin:2rem 0; }
  .zx8 .way{ border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.14);
    border-radius:1.2rem; padding:1.8rem 2rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
  .zx8 .way p{ opacity:.75; font-size:1.4rem; flex:1; }
  .zx8 .way .tag{ display:inline-block; align-self:flex-start; font-size:1.1rem;
    font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase;
    border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.25); border-radius:99rem;
    padding:.3rem 1rem; margin-bottom:1rem; opacity:.8; }
  .zx8 details{ border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.14);
    border-radius:1rem; padding:1.2rem 1.6rem; margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .zx8 summary{ font-weight:600; cursor:pointer; font-size:1.5rem; }
  .zx8 details p{ margin:.8rem 0 0; opacity:.78; font-size:1.45rem; }
  .zx8 .fine{ font-size:1.3rem; opacity:.65; margin:4rem 0 0;
    border-top:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.12); padding-top:1.6rem; }
  .zx8 .cta-row{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:1.2rem; margin:2rem 0; }

  /* --- business-inquiry form --- */
  .zx8 .biz{ max-width:76rem; margin:0 auto; }
  .zx8 .biz-lead{ opacity:.78; font-size:1.5rem; margin:0 0 2rem; }
  .zx8 .bizgrid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1.4rem; }
  .zx8 .bizgrid .span2{ grid-column:1 / -1; }
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px){
    .zx8 .bizgrid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
  }
  /* A <select> can't float Dawn's label the way text inputs do (no
     :placeholder-shown on selects), so pin its label in the "shrunk"
     position and pad the select to match a filled text field. */
  .zx8 .field--select .field__label{ font-size:1rem; top:.5rem;
    letter-spacing:.04em; }
  .zx8 .field--select select.field__input{ padding:2.2rem 1.5rem .8rem 2rem;
    width:100%; cursor:pointer; }
  .zx8 .biz-direct{ font-size:1.4rem; opacity:.75; margin:1.6rem 0 0; }
</style>

<div class="zx8" style="padding-bottom:5.6rem;">

  <div class="hero">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1600 700" role="img" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
         aria-label="Render of the Project Lightning controller board: a dark circuit board with gold traces and a lightning motif, carrying the words ZeroStick 8K Polling, Project Lightning, Built exclusively for PC, Now taking business orders">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="z8bg" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#0a0f1a"/>
          <stop offset=".55" stop-color="#080b12"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#04060a"/>
        </linearGradient>
        <linearGradient id="z8board" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#101826"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#0a111c"/>
        </linearGradient>
        <linearGradient id="z8bolt" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#bfe3ff"/>
          <stop offset=".5" stop-color="#58a6ff"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#1f6fd0"/>
        </linearGradient>
        <radialGradient id="z8glow" cx=".5" cy=".5" r=".5">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#58a6ff" stop-opacity=".35"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#58a6ff" stop-opacity="0"/>
        </radialGradient>
      </defs>

      <rect width="1600" height="700" fill="url(#z8bg)"/>

      <!-- the board, tilted, filling the left two-thirds -->
      <g transform="rotate(-8 450 350)">
        <rect x="-80" y="120" width="1000" height="520" rx="26"
              fill="url(#z8board)" stroke="#223047" stroke-width="2"/>
        <!-- gold traces -->
        <g stroke="#c9a86a" stroke-width="3" fill="none" opacity=".8"
           stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M20 200 H240 L300 260 H520"/>
          <path d="M20 260 H200 L260 320 H480 L520 360"/>
          <path d="M20 500 H180 L240 440 H460"/>
          <path d="M20 560 H300 L360 500 H560"/>
          <path d="M640 180 V300 L700 360 V520"/>
          <path d="M760 200 V280 L820 340 V480"/>
        </g>
        <!-- pads and vias -->
        <g fill="#c9a86a" opacity=".9">
          <circle cx="240" cy="200" r="7"/><circle cx="200" cy="260" r="7"/>
          <circle cx="180" cy="500" r="7"/><circle cx="300" cy="560" r="7"/>
          <circle cx="640" cy="180" r="7"/><circle cx="760" cy="200" r="7"/>
          <circle cx="520" cy="200" r="7"/><circle cx="560" cy="500" r="7"/>
        </g>
        <!-- stick-mechanism footprints -->
        <g stroke="#c9a86a" fill="none" stroke-width="3" opacity=".85">
          <circle cx="180" cy="360" r="58"/>
          <circle cx="180" cy="360" r="34"/>
          <circle cx="180" cy="360" r="10" fill="#c9a86a"/>
          <circle cx="620" cy="430" r="58"/>
          <circle cx="620" cy="430" r="34"/>
          <circle cx="620" cy="430" r="10" fill="#c9a86a"/>
        </g>
        <!-- the processor -->
        <g>
          <rect x="380" y="300" width="120" height="120" rx="8"
                fill="#05070c" stroke="#2c3b55" stroke-width="2"/>
          <g stroke="#c9a86a" stroke-width="3" opacity=".8">
            <path d="M380 320 h-24 M380 350 h-24 M380 380 h-24 M380 410 h-24"/>
            <path d="M500 320 h24 M500 350 h24 M500 380 h24 M500 410 h24"/>
          </g>
          <text x="440" y="352" text-anchor="middle" fill="#58a6ff"
                font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="17" font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="2">ZS-8K</text>
          <text x="440" y="378" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4a5a75"
                font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12"
                letter-spacing="1">LIGHTNING</text>
        </g>
        <!-- USB-C footprint -->
        <rect x="404" y="128" width="72" height="22" rx="11"
              fill="#05070c" stroke="#2c3b55" stroke-width="2"/>
        <!-- silkscreen -->
        <text x="40" y="620" fill="#3d4c66" font-family="Arial, sans-serif"
              font-size="15" letter-spacing="3">ZS-LTN-01 · DESIGNED BY ZEROSTICK</text>
      </g>

      <!-- lightning bolt striking the processor -->
      <ellipse cx="470" cy="330" rx="260" ry="200" fill="url(#z8glow)"/>
      <path d="M560 20 L470 240 L540 250 L400 470 L452 300 L384 290 Z"
            fill="url(#z8bolt)" opacity=".95"/>

      <!-- right-aligned wordmark block -->
      <g font-family="Arial, sans-serif" text-anchor="end">
        <text x="1540" y="210" fill="#8fa3c0" font-size="34"
              letter-spacing="10">ZEROSTICK · 8K POLLING</text>
        <text x="1540" y="320" fill="#f2f6fc" font-size="92" font-weight="700"
              letter-spacing="4">PROJECT</text>
        <text x="1540" y="424" fill="#58a6ff" font-size="92" font-weight="700"
              letter-spacing="4">LIGHTNING</text>
        <text x="1540" y="500" fill="#c9d5e8" font-size="30" letter-spacing="3">
          NATIVE 8K POLLING · ULTRA-LOW INPUT LATENCY</text>
        <text x="1540" y="556" fill="#58a6ff" font-size="30" font-weight="700"
              letter-spacing="4">BUILT EXCLUSIVELY FOR PC</text>
        <text x="1540" y="608" fill="#c9d5e8" font-size="26" letter-spacing="6">
          NOW TAKING BUSINESS ORDERS</text>
      </g>

      <!-- render tag (it's our own art, not a photograph) -->
      <g font-family="Arial, sans-serif">
        <rect x="28" y="640" width="190" height="34" rx="17" fill="none"
              stroke="#3d4c66" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="123" y="662" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fa3c0" font-size="15"
              letter-spacing="2">CONCEPT RENDER</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="inner">
    <div class="mission">
      <p><strong>The Lightning board is finished.</strong> Project Lightning is
      ZeroStick's own 8K controller board — designed in-house, from the traces
      up, and <strong>built exclusively for PC</strong>: native 8,000&nbsp;Hz
      polling, response measured in microseconds, and the drift-resistant TMR
      sticks our controllers are already known for.</p>
      <p>This page is for <strong>businesses that want the board itself</strong> —
      controller brands, modding shops, esports organizations and hardware
      companies who want Lightning in bulk, inside their own products, or on
      their own shelves. Tell us what you're building in the inquiry form
      below.</p>
      <p style="border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.25);
        border-left:.4rem solid #58a6ff; border-radius:.8rem;
        padding:1.2rem 1.6rem;"><strong>PC only.</strong> Lightning is not a
      console board — it does not connect to a PS5, Xbox or Switch, and it
      never will; consoles cap how fast any controller may report, which
      defeats the entire point of this board. Building for console players?
      The <a href="/pages/zerostick-exo">ZeroStick EXO</a> is the product
      line for that.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Built for exactly one thing</h2>
    <div class="strip">
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">⚡</div><h3>Native 8K polling</h3>
        <p>8,000 reports a second on PC — not overclocked, not software-forced.
        Native, from the board itself.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🎯</div><h3>TMR drift-free sticks</h3>
        <p>The same magnetic TMR stick technology in every ZeroStick build
        today — stable accuracy that doesn't wear into drift.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">⏱</div><h3>Microsecond response</h3>
        <p>Every part of the signal path chosen for speed. Nothing between
        your thumb and the game that doesn't have to be there.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🎮</div><h3>A shell you already know</h3>
        <p>Familiar controller in your hands — Lightning changes what's
        inside, not what you've spent years mastering.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>How we work with companies</h2>
    <div class="ways">
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">Bulk</span>
        <h3>Bulk board orders</h3>
        <p>Lightning boards in quantity for your own builds — bare boards or
        pre-wired kits, ready for your bench or production line.</p></div>
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">OEM</span>
        <h3>OEM integration</h3>
        <p>Put Lightning inside your own product. We work with your team on
        fit, firmware and branding.</p></div>
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">Resell</span>
        <h3>Reseller &amp; distribution</h3>
        <p>Carry ZeroStick 8K products in your store, catalog or region.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="#BizInquiry" class="button">Start a business inquiry</a>
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      The inquiry form. Shopify's built-in contact form: every field named
      contact[...] is emailed to the store inbox, so no app or backend is
      needed. Only the email field is required by Shopify.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="biz" id="BizInquiry">
      <h2>Business inquiries</h2>
      <p class="biz-lead">Tell us who you are, what you're building, and the
      volumes you have in mind — we answer every serious inquiry.</p>

      {%- form 'contact', id: 'BizInquiryForm', class: 'isolate' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <h3 class="form-status form-status-list form__message" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
            {{- 'icon-success.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            Thanks — your inquiry is in. We'll get back to you by email.
          </h3>
        {%- elsif form.errors -%}
          <div class="form__message">
            <h3 class="form-status caption-large text-body" role="alert" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              Please fix the highlighted field and send again.
            </h3>
          </div>
          <ul class="form-status-list caption-large" role="list">
            <li>
              <a href="#BizInquiry-email" class="link">
                {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
                {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="bizgrid">
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-company"
                   name="contact[Company]" autocomplete="organization"
                   placeholder="Company">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-company">Company</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-name"
                   name="contact[Name]" autocomplete="name"
                   value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name }}{% endif %}"
                   placeholder="Your name">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-name">Your name</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field field--with-error">
            <input class="field__input" type="email" id="BizInquiry-email"
                   name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false"
                   autocapitalize="off" aria-required="true" required
                   value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email }}{% endif %}"
                   {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
                     aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="BizInquiry-email-error"
                   {% endif %}
                   placeholder="Work email">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-email">Work email
              <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            {%- if form.errors contains 'email' -%}
              <small class="contact__field-error" id="BizInquiry-email-error">
                <span class="visually-hidden">Error</span>
                <span class="form__message">
                  <span class="svg-wrapper">
                    {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                  </span>
                  {{- form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
                  {{ form.errors.messages.email -}}
                </span>
              </small>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="tel" id="BizInquiry-phone"
                   name="contact[Phone]" autocomplete="tel"
                   placeholder="Phone (optional)">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-phone">Phone (optional)</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field field--select">
            <select class="field__input" id="BizInquiry-interest"
                    name="contact[Interested in]">
              <option value="Bulk board order">Bulk board order</option>
              <option value="OEM / build Lightning into our product">OEM — build Lightning into our product</option>
              <option value="Reseller / distribution">Reseller / distribution</option>
              <option value="Something else">Something else</option>
            </select>
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-interest">Interested in</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-qty"
                   name="contact[Estimated quantity]"
                   placeholder="Estimated quantity">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-qty">Estimated quantity</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field span2">
            <textarea rows="8" id="BizInquiry-body"
                      class="text-area field__input"
                      name="contact[Message]"
                      placeholder="Tell us about your project">{{- form.body -}}</textarea>
            <label class="form__label field__label" for="BizInquiry-body">
              Tell us about your project</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <button type="submit" class="button">Send inquiry</button>
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}

      <p class="biz-direct">Prefer direct?
        Email <a href="mailto:reliabletrendenterprises@gmail.com">reliabletrendenterprises@gmail.com</a>
        or text <a href="tel:+13236804706">(323) 680-4706</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Questions companies ask us</h2>
    <details><summary>What exactly can we buy?</summary>
      <p>The Lightning board itself (ZS-LTN-01) in quantity — bare boards or
      pre-wired kits — plus OEM work if you want it designed into your own
      product, and reseller terms for finished ZeroStick 8K controllers.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do you have order minimums?</summary>
      <p>No hard minimum to start the conversation. Tell us the volumes you
      have in mind and we'll quote around them — pricing and lead times are
      quoted per inquiry.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it work on console?</summary>
      <p><strong>No. Lightning is a PC-only board.</strong> It does not
      connect to a PS5, Xbox or Switch — consoles cap how fast any controller
      may report, and an 8K board inside a capped console would be a fast
      engine behind a closed gate. We would rather say that plainly than sell
      you boards for the wrong machine. Building for console players? Ask us
      about the <a href="/pages/zerostick-exo">ZeroStick EXO</a> line instead.</p></details>
    <details><summary>I'm a gamer, not a company — can I still get one?</summary>
      <p>Yes — finished 8K controllers built on Lightning are coming to the
      store. The fastest way to hear the moment they're live is the
      <a href="/pages/contact">contact page</a>.</p></details>

    <p class="fine">Business pricing, specifications and lead times are quoted
    per inquiry and may change. The board image above is a render of our own
    design, not a photograph. DualSense and DualShock are trademarks of Sony
    Interactive Entertainment; Xbox is a trademark of Microsoft. ZeroStick
    modifies genuine first-party hardware and is not affiliated with or
    endorsed by Sony or Microsoft.</p>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ZS 8K Business Inquiries",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "ZS 8K Business Inquiries"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
